	(text "Front Panel\nTFT display (shares the SPI bus), rotary encoder with push button.\nHardware FAULT LED driven directly from FAULT_EXT - works without the MCU."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "400126b2-4467-4685-a6b4-debc090af36d")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- Display: SPI TFT on the shared SPI bus, own DISP_CS and DISP_DC, backlight control input driven from DISP_BL (PWM dimming).\n- Rotary encoder with push button: pull-ups + RC debounce.\n- FAULT LED (red) driven directly from FAULT_EXT (24 V) through a resistor - works without the MCU.\n- New aluminium front plate. Keep cutouts for the main switch Q1 (wired to PL1) and the t> potentiometer of 3N2.\n- Decided: one board behind the front plate (like the old PL2); display module and encoder mount on it.\n- No touch screen: the rotary encoder is the only input. Optional later: buzzer for alarms.\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- Display: 3.5 in IPS 480x320, ST7796S controller, SPI module. Alt: 2.8 in 320x240 ILI9341 (cheaper, smaller).\n- Encoder: Alps EC11 series with push switch (EC11E series). Debounce 10k / 10 nF.\n- FAULT LED: 5 mm red panel LED, 4.7k series resistor (~5 mA at 24 V).\n- Backlight: no external switch - the module LED pin is a control input (LCDWiki)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 20.32 0)
		(size 152.4 40)
		(margins 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6b8ecfd1-170f-43e8-8e07-b3c91e82ccf2")
	)
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
